# Git push safety

- **Never** `git push` to `main` / `master` unless the user explicitly asks to push (or to deploy via pushing `main`).
- **Never** auto-push after a commit, even if the change is ready and CI would deploy on push.
- Only `git commit` when the user explicitly asks to commit (same as existing commit rules).
- If work is done and deploy needs a push, tell the user the branch is ready and ask whether to push — do not push first.

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD: commit then immediately `git push origin main`
❌ BAD: push "to apply" a workflow/feature without being asked
✅ GOOD: commit only if asked; stop and say "ready to push when you want"
✅ GOOD: `git push origin main` only after user says e.g. "push lên main" / "push đi"
```
